---
# Machine-readable index of every published book page. Client JS (e.g. My
# Library's genre recommendations) fetches this instead of needing a backend
# endpoint — the data is already public in the static pages themselves.
layout: null
permalink: /books.json
---
[
{% comment %} gutenberg_id (null when the book has no free Gutenberg text) is
   what the API repo's warm-print workflow reads to know which books have a
   printable edition to push to R2. It belongs here rather than in a second
   list because this file is already the answer to "which books exist and what
   do we know about them" — a separate list would be a second source of truth
   to keep in step by hand, which is how the Firestore rules drifted for three
   weeks. {% endcomment %}
{% for book in site.books %}  { "title": {{ book.title | jsonify }}, "author": {{ book.author | jsonify }}, "url": {{ book.url | relative_url | jsonify }}, "cover_url": {{ book.cover_url | jsonify }}, "categories": {{ book.categories | jsonify }}, "gutenberg_id": {{ book.free_ebook.gutenberg_id | jsonify }} }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{% endfor %}]
